    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7451" root="حذق" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَذِيقٌ</span></b>  (S, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْذُوقٌ</span></b>  (K) <i>Cut:</i> (S,
K, * TA:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْذَاقٌ</span>. (Lh, TA.) One says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَبْلٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْذَاقٌ</span> <i>A rope altogether worn out; as though
it were cut:</i> (Lh, K, * TA:) every part of it
being termed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَذِيق</span>. (Lh, TA.)

